# A weekly cron job (Sunday 03:00) that always targets _monthly, on a pool that
# keeps only three monthlies. Uploads must land about once a month, on the first
# Sunday after each 1st, as an INCR from the previous monthly; every run in
# between is a NOOP. The monthly two back is still on the pool when each
# incremental runs (sanoid destroys a monthly once it is older than 3*31 days
# AND more than three remain), so the chain never breaks, and the fulls roll
# on the first Sunday after the first 1st past each 4320h window.
volume=backup3/enc/user/app/navidrome
location=America/New_York
policy=hourly=48,daily=30,monthly=3
from=2026-09-27T03:00:00
until=2027-10-10T03:00:00
every=168h
checks=coverage:_monthly          # every monthly backed up exactly once
